<title>USA: N-Viro International Corp Q3 shr rises.</title>
<headline>N-Viro International Corp Q3 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>TOLEDO, Ohio 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							   Sept. 30,</p>
<p>						    1996		1995</p>
<p> Revenues				  $1,421,463	$1,300,658</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			  136,624	     7,257</p>
<p> Net shr (loss)				  0.07		0.00</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>   shares outstanding		   2,037,000	 2,037,000</p>
<p>							Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>							   Sept. 30,</p>
<p>						     1996	     1995</p>
<p> Revenues				  $3,370,738	$4,266,487</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			  272,679	 (905,526)</p>
<p> Net shr (loss)				  0.13	    (0.44)</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>   shares outstanding		   2,037,000	 2,037,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Per share comparisons have been restated to reflect a one-for-four reverse common stock split on October 31, 1995.</p>
<p>Company said Q3 1996 profit reflects the results of improved licensing fees for the quarter as well as a continuation of cost containment programs.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
